.TH LANDFILL 1 "2026-10-14" "landfill 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
landfill \- assembler for core RV32I instructions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B landfill
.RB [ \-s | \-st | \-\-symboltable ]
.I file
.br
.B landfill \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B landfill
assembles the RV32I base integer instructions in
.I file
into raw machine code. The machine code is \fBnot\fR in any particular format.
The output is written next to the input with its extension replaced by
.BR .bin ;
for example,
.I prog.asm
produces
.IR prog.bin .
.PP
Each instruction becomes a 32-bit little-endian word.
Pseudoinstructions and assembler directives are not yet supported.
.PP
If assembly fails, no output file is written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-st ", " \-\-symboltable
Print the symbol table to standard output after assembling,
one label per line followed by its address in hexadecimal.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The file could not be read or written, or contains an error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
Assemble
.I riscv.asm
into
.I riscv.bin
and print its labels:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ landfill \-s riscv.asm
loop 0x00000000
end 0x00000008
.EE
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
batteryspecial (batteryspecial.xyz)
